WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:12.236
Hi I'm Jack, I'm from the great city of Norwich in the UK that I'm actually talking from the middle of Tokyo in the early hours.
大家好，我是杰克，我来自英国伟大的城市诺维奇，但我其实是在清晨的东京市中心和大家说话。

00:00:12.236 --> 00:00:15.166
What how I make a mother means to me?
“老爸老妈罗曼史”对我意味着什么？

00:00:15.166 --> 00:00:29.579
It's the emphasis on hindsight, the benefit of hindsight and the fact that as bleak and as negative as things may seem in the moment, actually it may be building to something better.
那就是对后见之明的强调，事后诸葛亮的好处，以及这样一个事实：无论当下看起来多么惨淡、多么消极，实际上它可能在为更好的事情做铺垫。

00:00:29.579 --> 00:00:35.396
made me set me new on a course in your life, which ultimately leads something better.
让我踏上了生活中的新旅程，最终通向更好的事物。

00:00:35.396 --> 00:00:41.280
That means a lot, simply because I, about eight months ago, I had a nervous breakdown.
这意义重大，仅仅因为我，大约八个月前，我精神崩溃了。

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.538
I wasn't very happy with my life.
我对自己的生活很不满意。

00:00:43.538 --> 00:00:49.218
And here I am eight months now, I'm from that now, and I'm much happier where I am.
而现在八个月过去了，我走出了那段阴影，我对现在的状态满意多了。

00:00:49.218 --> 00:00:56.539
I'm in Tokyo for the first time, and I might be in a position to tell the girl that I love that I love her.
我生平第一次来到东京，我或许有机会对我爱的女孩表白。

00:00:56.539 --> 00:01:49.060
so and actually seriously thank you for that it's really helped thinking about it and watching the program I don't think you can be emphasised just how much it means to people and how much it means to me I don't know how to thank you for that except for this message Well, hello there, I'm Josh Ratner, I am joined by my friend Craig Thomas for another episode of How We Made Your Mother, Hi Craig.
所以，真的很感谢你，这真的很有帮助，通过思考和观看节目，怎么强调它对人们的意义以及对我个人的意义都不为过，我不知道该怎么感谢你，除了发这条信息。嗨，大家好，我是乔什·拉德纳，我的朋友克雷格·托马斯也加入了我的节目，带来又一期《老爸老妈罗曼史》，嗨，克雷格。

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:50.060
Hey Josh.
嗨，乔什。

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:51.060
Hey.
嗨。

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.060
Boy.
天哪。

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:59.340
I don't, maybe one of these openings won't, well, I won't get choked up as it's happening, but I'm 0 for 12 or whatever it is, and not getting choked up.
我不知道，也许有一次开场我不会在事情发生时哽咽，但我现在是12次全有去无回，每次都还是会哽咽。

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:04.340
It's always an amazing way to start the show because this is our first time hearing them.
以这种方式开始节目总是令人惊叹，因为这是我们第一次听到这些留言。

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.780
So it kind of puts you on your back foot in a good way, right?
所以这有点让你措手不及，但却是种美妙的体验，对吧？

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:12.300
like, I don't come on knowing what we're going to hear, how I'm going to respond to it.
就像，我来的时候并不知道我们会听到什么，我会有什么反应。

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:16.020
What Jack was saying so, so beautifully.
杰克刚才说得真是太美妙了。

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:48.750
And I think the thing about, I think the medicine, if you could distill what, how I met your mother, the special medicine that it has within it, that people keep going back to it as if it's some kind of like, well, or altar, some sort of like nourishing, life-giving thing, is It doesn't shy away from the low moments, but it gives you this context for viewing the tough stuff in life that says, no, you know, a lot of times you have to be broken, open, so something else can come in.
而且我认为关于……如果你能提炼出《老爸老妈罗曼史》所蕴含的特殊药方，那种让人们不断回头重温，仿佛它是某种源泉、某种圣坛，某种充满滋养、给予生命的事物的力量，那就是它并不回避低谷，但它为你提供了一个看待生活中艰难时刻的视角，告诉你，不，你知道吗，很多时候你必须先碎裂、敞开，好让别的东西进来。

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:56.030
And the old parts of you have to die and go away and wither before the new thing can regenerate and grow.
你旧的部分必须死去、消散并枯萎，新的事物才能再生和成长。

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:04.150
And you know, I was listening to him and I was like, wow, I need to hear this today.
你知道的，我听着他的话，心想，哇，我今天真需要听到这些。

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.469
Like, I'm glad you said that, you know?
就像，很高兴你这么说了，你知道吗？

00:03:06.469 --> 00:03:07.310
Me too.
我也是。

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:17.389
And I'm just, as you know, winding down my tour and I have certain songs that I'm so glad I wrote them because I get to sing them all the time and I get to hear them again.
正如你所知，我的巡演正接近尾声，有些歌曲我庆幸自己写了它们，因为我可以一直唱它们，还能再次听到它们。

00:03:17.389 --> 00:03:19.629
I get to hear them anew.
我能以全新的方式听到它们。

00:03:19.629 --> 00:03:42.107
And even working on this show with you, Craig and Alec and everyone else is like, it's just refreshing that message within me, you know, and it's so much, it's bigger than how I your mother, but I think how I met your mother did such a good job at creating, spinning a narrative where people could get, you know, literally punched in the face.
甚至和你、克雷格、亚历克以及其他所有人一起制作这部剧，也让我内心深处的信息焕然一新，你知道的，这意义重大，它超越了《老爸老妈罗曼史》本身，但我认为《老爸老妈罗曼史》在创造、编织一个叙事方面做得太棒了，让人们在经历生活重击（字面意义上的当头棒喝）时……

00:03:42.107 --> 00:03:44.270
It was all part of some big plan.
这一切都是某个宏大计划的一部分。

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:46.634
I mean, it's really, it's quite magical.
我的意思是，这真的很神奇。

00:03:46.634 --> 00:03:47.994
Well, it's interesting.
嗯，这很有趣。

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:50.122
There's this idea of the one, right?
这里有一个关于“真命天子/女”的概念，对吧？

00:03:50.122 --> 00:03:52.309
I'm going to hold on to meet the one.
我要坚持下去，直到遇到那个对的人。

00:03:52.309 --> 00:03:54.496
And that is a beautiful thing, right?
这是一件美好的事情，对吧？

00:03:54.496 --> 00:03:57.747
That aspiration, that romantic idea of meeting the one.
那种对遇到真爱的高贵追求、浪漫想法。

00:03:57.747 --> 00:04:10.338
But what I took from Jack's message, and I think it is in the show too, maybe even as much or more built into the structure of the show, is that when you're in a low moment, you should also hold on for future you.
但我从杰克的留言中领悟到，而且我认为这在剧中也有体现，甚至可能更多地构建在剧集的结构中，那就是当你处于低谷时，你也应该为未来的自己坚持下去。

00:04:10.338 --> 00:04:12.170
That's who you're doing it for.
那就是你为之奋斗的目标。

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:16.131
You're holding out an enduring for them so they can get through it.
你为了他们而坚持、忍耐，这样他们就能挺过难关。

00:04:16.131 --> 00:04:17.550
You can meet them later.
你以后会遇到他们。

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:20.017
You can meet future you and tell the story.
你可以遇见未来的自己并讲述这个故事。

00:04:20.017 --> 00:04:21.451
That's who you owe it to.
这是你对未来的承诺。

00:04:21.451 --> 00:04:23.230
That's who you're doing it for.
这就是你为之奋斗的动力。

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:27.550
And it's almost like future me is gonna need some resilience.
这就像未来的我将需要一些韧性。

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:32.100
They're gonna need the lessons and strength that I'm gathering now.
他们需要我现在正在收集的教训和力量。

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.300
Because it might even be harder in the future.
因为未来可能会更加艰难。

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:38.939
It's like, I need to, I'm in training for my future self.
这就好像，我需要，我正在为未来的自己进行训练。

00:04:38.939 --> 00:04:48.019
And presumably maybe your kids, I think there's that kind of like, there's the storyline of parents' sacrifice for their children.
当然也许还有你的孩子们，我认为这其中有一种……父母为孩子牺牲的故事线。

00:04:48.019 --> 00:04:49.899
And we sacrifice for our future selves.
而我们为未来的自己牺牲。

00:04:49.899 --> 00:04:52.540
Like it's a really, that's quite a lovely idea.
这真的是一个非常美好的想法。

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.290
I love that, Craig.
我喜欢这个观点，克雷格。

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:57.930
Yeah, I mean, I really heard that in what Jack said there.
是的，我的意思是，我在杰克刚才的话里深深地听到了这一点。

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.250
So, Jack, thank you.
所以，杰克，谢谢你。

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:03.689
Thanks for reminding us of that part of the show we made that maybe we weren't aware of at the time in a way.
谢谢你提醒我们节目中那部分我们当初可能并没有完全意识到的意义。

00:05:03.689 --> 00:05:10.449
And also like, how I met your mother is very much about a man in dialogue with himself.
还有就是，《老爸老妈浪漫史》在很大程度上是一个男人与自己的对话。

00:05:10.449 --> 00:05:30.213
Yeah, it is that there's a, certainly the older narrator Ted is in dialogue with this younger self, but on some cosmic weird level, present day Ted, My Ted, the Ted I played, is also in dialogue with his older self because he's always thinking about the front porch down the line and what I'm going to be.
对，确实是这样，年长的旁白泰德在和年轻的自己对话，但在某种奇怪的宇宙层面上，当下的泰德，也就是我，我所扮演的泰德，其实也在和年老的自己对话，因为他总是想着未来的前廊，想着自己将来会成为什么样的人。

00:05:30.213 --> 00:05:32.934
He's trying to lay the seeds for his life.
他正为自己的人生播下种子。

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:40.256
And he's mistake prone and he draws erroneous conclusions quite a bit, but he ultimately does string it together.
他会犯错，也经常得出错误的结论，但他最终还是把这一切串联了起来。

00:05:40.256 --> 00:05:44.663
And I think there's something about the show that's quite forgiving.
我觉得这部剧有一种非常宽容的特质。

00:05:44.663 --> 00:05:55.873
There's a mercy at the heart of it that I think people really respond to like it's okay to make mistakes, it's okay to, you know, it's okay to have a breakdown as Jack said.
它的核心有一种仁慈，我觉得观众对此很有共鸣，比如犯错是没关系的，你知道的，像杰克说的，崩溃一下也是没关系的。

00:05:55.873 --> 00:06:03.001
And then before, you know, eight months, eight months is not that long to kind of like swing to the other way.
而且你看，八个月前的事，八个月其实并不算太长，就能发生这样的大逆转。

00:06:03.001 --> 00:06:05.333
So it's like, it gives people faith.
所以这让人重燃希望。

00:06:05.333 --> 00:06:09.739
I mean, what better thing would you hope for from a television show?
我的意思是，你能从一部电视剧里期望更好的东西吗？

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:16.987
Yeah, it's an honor and a privilege to hear that it meant that to Jack and other people, it's amazing.
是的，听说这部剧对杰克和其他人有这样的意义，我深感荣幸和特权，这太棒了。

00:06:16.987 --> 00:06:20.017
And that is the aspirational quality of the show.
这也是这部剧所具有的追求和向往的特质。

00:06:20.017 --> 00:06:34.795
It seems at first that it's the aspiration of meeting the one, but in a way it's also just surviving and telling, realizing you're becoming the person who's going to tell this story one day, which I loved head for because that's his drive.
起初看起来，这种追求是遇到真爱，但从某种程度上说，它也只是一种生存和倾诉，意识到自己正在成为那个终有一天会讲述这个故事的人，我非常喜欢泰德这一点，因为那是他的动力。

00:06:34.795 --> 00:06:36.279
That's really his drive.
那确实是他的动力。

00:06:36.279 --> 00:06:36.779
Yeah.
对。

00:06:36.779 --> 00:06:41.465
Well, let's downshift into the episode under discussion this week.
好了，让我们把节奏慢下来，进入我们本周要讨论的剧集。

00:06:41.319 --> 00:06:44.019
This episode embodies a lot of what we just talked about.
这一集完美体现了我们刚刚谈到的大部分内容。

00:06:44.019 --> 00:06:45.319
Yeah, it really does.
对，确实如此。

00:06:45.319 --> 00:06:47.720
And this is kind of, we've been talking about this.
而且，我们之前也一直在讨论这个。

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:56.519
This is kind of part one of a really like a two-part episode around this wedding, this episode, the wedding, which is episode 12, is that right, Alec?
这集实际上是关于这场婚礼的上下两集里的第一部分，也就是第12集，对吧，亚历克？

00:06:56.519 --> 00:06:57.019
Yes.
是的。

00:06:57.019 --> 00:06:57.575
Yeah.
对。

